#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:4
msgid "Selective Sync"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:6
msgid ""
"This is for when you don't want to synchronize *all* files from the cluster "
"onto your device, or you want only some directories of yours to be synced "
"*to* the cluster. There are two mechanisms that support this usage; "
"*Directory Selection* and *Excluded Files*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:13
msgid "Directory Selection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:15
msgid ""
"By default, all directories in a given folder are synchronized. Using "
"directory selection, the synchronization can be limited to a subset of "
"directories. The selection is done by using a tree browser. The tree "
"represents the cluster wide contents of a folder. The default is represented "
"by the top level being checked and directories underneath the top level thus "
"being implicitly included::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:22
msgid ""
"[X] ~/Sync\n"
"    [ ] Documents\n"
"        [ ] Processes\n"
"        [ ] Standards\n"
"    [ ] Pictures\n"
"        [ ] Vacation\n"
"        [ ] Work\n"
"    [ ] Music\n"
"        [ ] Classical\n"
"        [ ] Rock"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:33
msgid ""
"To only synchronize documents and vacation pictures, the following selection "
"can be made::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:35
msgid ""
"[/] ~/Sync\n"
"    [X] Documents\n"
"        [ ] Processes\n"
"        [ ] Standards\n"
"    [/] Pictures\n"
"        [X] Vacation\n"
"        [ ] Work\n"
"    [ ] Music\n"
"        [ ] Classical\n"
"        [ ] Rock"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:46
msgid ""
"The top level shows a partial checkbox to indicate that selections have been "
"made at a lower level. With this configuration Syncthing will ignore any "
"files and directories no in ~/Sync/Documents or ~/Sync/Pictures/Vacation -- "
"no changes will be downloaded from the cluster and local changes will not be "
"tracked."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:52
msgid ""
"When displaying the tree we must merge what we actually have on disk with "
"what is in the global state, or we will not be able to show new directories "
"to the user as we don't know about them..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:58
msgid "Excluded Files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:60
msgid ""
"In addition to using directory selection, specific files can be excluded by "
"adding patterns to match them. Excluded files are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:63
msgid ""
"Ignored when found on disk (i.e. not hashed and not announced to other "
"devices)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:66
msgid ""
"Ignored when announced by other devices (i.e. will not contribute to an "
"\"out of sync\" status or be fetched from the network)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:69
msgid ""
"*Removed* when present in a directory that is marked for deletion by another "
"device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:72
msgid ""
"Patterns are in \"glob\" form, with the following allowed syntax elements:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:74
msgid "Asterisk (``*``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:75
msgid "Matches zero or more characters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:77
msgid "Question mark (``?``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:78
msgid "Matches exactly one character."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:80
msgid "Ranges (``[a-f]``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:81
msgid "Matches any of the characters in the range exactly once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:83
msgid "Exclamation mark (``!``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:84
msgid ""
"At the start of a pattern, inverts the pattern (i.e. make matched file *not* "
"be excluded)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:86
msgid "Examples:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:88
msgid "``*.jpg``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:89
msgid "Matches all files with the ``jpg`` extension."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:91
msgid "``[0-9]*``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:92
msgid "Matches all files with names starting with a digit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:94
msgid "``!*.doc``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:95
msgid "Do not exclude ``.doc`` files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:97
msgid ""
"File exclusions apply only to files, not to directories, and apply equally "
"in all directories in the folder. Patterns are searched in the order given "
"and the first match wins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:103
msgid "Use Cases"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:105
msgid "Sync only specific directories"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:106
msgid "This is covered perfectly by the \"directory selection\" part"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:108
msgid "Exclude common crap files like Thumbs.db"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:109
msgid "This is covered perfectly by the \"excluded files\" part"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:111
msgid "Sync only a specific file type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:112
msgid "Covered by ``!``-pattern plus exclude everything"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:114
msgid "Exclude a specific directory only"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:115
msgid ""
"Possible by using directory selection and selecting all other directories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:117
msgid ""
"Sync only a specific file in a specific directory; i.e. only one movie out "
"of lots"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../draft/selective.rst:118
msgid "Not really possible... Do we need this?"
msgstr ""

